  "description": "Catskill peaks over 3,500 feet. Membership in the Catskill 3500 Club requires the listed peaks plus four of them repeated in winter.",
  "criteria": "Catskill peaks of at least 3,500 ft on the club's tally list. Traditionally 35 peaks; since 2021 the club's required list is 33 (Graham and Doubletop closed to the public). All 35 are included here. Elevations for the 33 are the club's published figures; Graham and Doubletop use Wikipedia's figures.",
  "organization": "Catskill 3500 Club",
  "officialUrl": "https://www.catskill3500club.org/",
  "notes": "The traditional list is 35 peaks, but per the club's current website the required list is 33: Graham and Doubletop were closed to public access effective Jan 13, 2021 (South Doubletop and Millbrook Ridge were briefly required and dropped Mar 22, 2021). They are kept here as the traditional 35 and flagged in their notes; the app may treat them as optional. Winter requirement: members must ALSO climb Slide, Blackhead, Balsam and Panther in winter (peaks marked 'winter-required'), giving 33 + 4 = 37 climbs under the current list (39 under the old 35). The club by-laws define winter as December 21 through March 21 inclusive, regardless of actual solstice/equinox dates; you need only be on the summit in that window. Winter patch list: a separate award, earned after basic membership, for climbing all of the required peaks (33 under the current list) in winter (Dec 21 to Mar 21). The app should track a per-ascent winter flag so both the 4 required winter peaks and the full winter-patch list can be computed. Ranges are common groupings, not from the club. Coordinates from OpenStreetMap peak nodes. Slide (4185) and Hunter (4030) use the club's figures; Wikipedia shows 4180 and 4040.",
  "sources": [
